s east of Legio, near mount Tabor, and, according to D'Arvieux, about eight leagues, or according to Maundrell, seven hours, or about twenty miles S. E. of Acre. It is one of the principal towns of the pashalic of Acre, containing a population of about 3,000 souls, of whom 500 are Turks, the remainder being Christians. It is delightfully situated on elevated ground, in a valley, encompassed by mountains.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-40","title":"Luke 2:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>the child. 52; Jud 13:24; 1Sa 2:18,26; 3:19; Ps 22:9; Isa 53:1,2 strong. 1:80; Eph 6:10; 2Ti 2:1 filled. 47,52; Isa 11:1-5; Col 2:2,3 the grace. Ps 45:2; Joh 1:14; Ac 4:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-41","title":"Luke 2:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>A.M. 4012. A.D. 8. went. Ex 23:14-17; 34:23; De 12:5-7,11,18; 16:1-8,16; 1Sa 1:3,21 the. Ex 12:14; Le 23:5; Nu 28:16; Joh 2:13; 6:4; 11:55; 13:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-43","title":"Luke 2:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>2Ch 30:21-23; 25:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-44","title":"Luke 2:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>in. Ps 42:4; 122:1-4; Isa 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-46","title":"Luke 2:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>after. 44,45; 1Ki 12:5,12; Mt 12:40; 16:21; 27:63,64 the doctors. 5:17; Ac 5:34 both. Isa 49:1,2; 50:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-2-47","title":"Luke 2:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>4:22,32; Ps 119:99; Mt 7